+# SPEC: Elevate RMG068 default severity to Warning
+
+## Objective
+When Mapperly cannot inline a user-implemented mapping method into a queryable
+projection (`IQueryable` / `Expression<Func<..>>`), EF Core falls back to
+client-side evaluation. Today this is only reported as `Info` (RMG068), which is
+easy to miss. Raise the default severity to `Warning` so it is visible and can
+be promoted to an error (`TreatWarningsAsErrors` / `.editorconfig`).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- `DiagnosticDescriptors.QueryableProjectionMappingCannotInline` (RMG068) has
+  `DefaultSeverity = Warning`.
+- `AnalyzerReleases.Unshipped.md` records the change under "Changed Rules".
+- Docs (`docs/docs/configuration/queryable-projections.mdx`) mention that it is
+  a warning and how to change its severity.
+- Snapshot tests updated; full test suite passes.
+
+## Commands
+- Build: `dotnet build`
+- Test: `dotnet test test/Riok.Mapperly.Tests`
+
+## Boundaries
+- Always: keep diagnostic id/title/message unchanged.
+- Never: change inlining behaviour itself.
